<title>THAILAND: Bank of Ayudhya to issue $150 mln bonds.</title>
<headline>Bank of Ayudhya to issue $150 mln bonds.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank of Ayudhya Plc said on Wednesday the bank will issue 10-year subordinated bonds worth $150 million in the U.S. market.</p>
<p>Bank of Ayudhya said in a filing to the Stock Exchange of Thailand that the bond issue, expected to be launched in July, is part of its Global Medium Term Note Programme.  </p>
<p>J.P. Morgan Co &amp; Inc was appointed as lead manager for the issue and Merrill Lynch and Salomon Brothers were mandated as co-lead managers, the bank said.</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
</text>
